    "text": "Suppose K < H < F are free groups of finite rank such that rank(H) <\nrank(K), but all proper subgroups of H which contain K have ranks ⩾ rank(K).\nThen is the inclusion of H in F the only homomorphism H → F fixing all elements\nof K?                                                           G. M. Bergman",
